{"summary":"Task suite-green-pm-helpers.2.3 requires covering a stricter unscoped-SQL-deletion guard rule in guard_shell.py with tests. The acceptance criteria specify: denying an unscoped deletion followed by another statement; denying an unscoped deletion chained with '&& echo ok'; allowing a deletion scoped by WHERE; asserting the current behavior for grep-pattern cases; maintaining equality between lane-stack/hooks/guard_shell.py and the bundled copy in src/native-hook-sources.ts; and ensuring both Vitest (tests/guard-lane-pilot-ship.test.ts, tests/guard.test.ts, tests/native-session-hooks.test.ts) and typecheck pass.

The provided excerpt contains lines 1 through 481 of lane-stack/hooks/guard_shell.py. This portion establishes the shell guard's structure: agent role classification (PM_AGENTS, LANE_PILOT_PM_AGENT_TYPES, LANE_PILOT_HELPER_ROLES), permitted command sets (LANE_PILOT_READ_COMMANDS, PM_READ_COMMANDS, PM_BB_READ_COMMANDS, PM_BB_MESSAGE_COMMANDS, LANE_PILOT_BB_COMMANDS, PM_CONTROL_COMMANDS, PM_OPS_COMMANDS), and edit restrictions via _pm_edit_allowed. It defines control shell tokens (_CONTROL_TOKENS = {';', '&&', '||', '|', '&', '(', ')', ';;', '|&'}), heredoc stripping (_without_data_heredocs), command argument unwrapping for sudo and env, permanent deletion detection (_delete_commands, _delete_targets, _permanent_delete_error), and a SQL mutation regex (SQL_MUTATION) matching keywords including 'delete'. It also contains _safe_psql checking queries supplied to psql via -c/--command.

However, the excerpt ends mid-function in _pm_segment_error and omits lines 482 through 1243 of lane-stack/hooks/guard_shell.py, which contain the actual unscoped-SQL-deletion guard rule implementation. Furthermore, neither tests/guard-lane-pilot-ship.test.ts, tests/guard.test.ts, tests/native-session-hooks.test.ts, nor src/native-hook-sources.ts are included in the execution packet.","keyFacts":["lane-stack/hooks/guard_shell.py: SQL_MUTATION is a case-insensitive regex matching insert, update, delete, merge, create, alter, drop, truncate, grant, revoke, comment, vacuum, reindex, cluster, and refresh.","lane-stack/hooks/guard_shell.py: _safe_psql disallows psql invocations using -f/--file or any -c/--command query matching the SQL_MUTATION regex.","lane-stack/hooks/guard_shell.py: _CONTROL_TOKENS is defined as {';', '&&', '||', '|', '&', '(', ')', ';;', '|&'}.","lane-stack/hooks/guard_shell.py: _delete_commands lexes shell commands with shlex using punctuation_chars=';&|()' and segments them across control tokens to check deletion targets.","lane-stack/hooks/guard_shell.py: _without_data_heredocs strips heredocs fed into non-shell commands so heredoc data is not treated as shell command tokens.","lane-stack/hooks/guard_shell.py: _pm_segment_error forbids mutating actions in find (-delete, -exec, etc.), in-place sed (-i, --in-place), and sort with output files (-o, --output).","lane-stack/hooks/guard_shell.py: Agent roles are partitioned into PM_AGENTS, LANE_PILOT_PM_AGENT_TYPES, and LANE_PILOT_HELPER_ROLES, with specific read and control sets.","lane-stack/hooks/guard_shell.py: _pm_edit_allowed blocks direct edits to source code, restricting PM edits to control-plane docs, .env secret files, chat scratch files, and run check.py scripts."],"openQuestions":["What is the exact implementation and regex/logic of the unscoped-SQL-deletion guard rule in lines 482-1243 of lane-stack/hooks/guard_shell.py?","How does the unscoped-SQL-deletion guard rule currently handle or distinguish grep/rg commands searching for SQL delete patterns versus actual SQL executions?","Does guard_shell.py already block unscoped deletions chained with other statements or '&& echo ok', or does the rule implementation itself need adjustments alongside new tests?","How are tests structured in tests/guard-lane-pilot-ship.test.ts and tests/native-session-hooks.test.ts, and what testing patterns or harness do they use for guard_shell.py payloads?","How is the bundled copy of guard_shell.py in src/native-hook-sources.ts structured and kept identical to lane-stack/hooks/guard_shell.py?"]}
